IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `au-part4-more`

-- Tests for s 11A. Expected values are written from the text: the position of an item is the number of existing items that come
-- before it when the letters alone are compared (spaces and hyphens ignored).

§ `Section 11A(1): a definition inserted with no position specified`

`some terms` MEANS LIST "affidavit", "Australia", "business day", "oath"

-- "Australian citizen" falls after "Australia" (a-u-s-t-r-a-l-i-a before a-u-s-t-r-a-l-i-a-n) and before "business day": position 2.
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` FALSE `some terms` "Australian citizen" EQUALS JUST 2
-- Before everything: "acting SES employee" (a-c ... before a-f).
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` FALSE `some terms` "acting SES employee" EQUALS JUST 0
-- After everything: "writing".
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` FALSE `some terms` "writing" EQUALS JUST 4
-- Between "business day" and "oath": "calendar month" (position 3).
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` FALSE `some terms` "calendar month" EQUALS JUST 3
-- Case does not matter, and letter-by-letter ignores the space: "Business-Day" is the same letters as "business day".
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` FALSE `some terms` "Business-Day" EQUALS NOTHING
-- A space is not a letter: "au stralia" has the letters of "australia".
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` FALSE `some terms` "au stralia" EQUALS NOTHING
-- The amending Act specifies the position: the section does not decide.
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` TRUE `some terms` "calendar month" EQUALS NOTHING
-- No existing definitions: the new one goes first.
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted definition among the definitions, counting from 0` FALSE EMPTY "calendar month" EQUALS JUST 0

§ `Section 11A(2): an item inserted into a list or table that was arranged alphabetically`

`an alphabetical list` MEANS LIST "Chair", "Chairman", "Chairperson", "Chairwoman"
`a list not in alphabetical order` MEANS LIST "Chairman", "Chair", "Chairwoman"

#ASSERT `the items are arranged alphabetically, letter by letter` `an alphabetical list`
#ASSERT NOT (`the items are arranged alphabetically, letter by letter` `a list not in alphabetical order`)
-- Letters "chairs": after chair, chairman (m before s) and chairperson (p before s), before chairwoman (s before w): position 3.
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted item among the items, counting from 0` FALSE `an alphabetical list` "Chairs" EQUALS JUST 3
-- "Chair" has the same letters as the existing "Chair": the text gives no position for an equal item.
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted item among the items, counting from 0` FALSE `an alphabetical list` "Chair" EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Deputy Chair" goes last.
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted item among the items, counting from 0` FALSE `an alphabetical list` "Deputy Chair" EQUALS JUST 4
-- The list was not arranged alphabetically immediately before the insertion: (b) fails and the section does not decide.
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted item among the items, counting from 0` FALSE `a list not in alphabetical order` "Chairs" EQUALS NOTHING
-- The amending Act specifies the position.
#ASSERT `the position of the inserted item among the items, counting from 0` TRUE `an alphabetical list` "Chairs" EQUALS NOTHING
